Assume the hypotheses and unpack their components. Rewrite the indicated hypotheses using the stated equalities. Extract witnesses or component facts from the available result. Reduce the conclusion to the remaining proof obligations. Apply function extensionality and compare values at an arbitrary argument.

Reduce the conclusion to the remaining proof obligations. Introduce a local definition for the expression. Establish an intermediate fact. Establish an intermediate fact. Reduce the claim to the hypotheses of an applicable result.

Assume the hypotheses and unpack their components. Establish an intermediate fact. By extensionality, compare the relevant components. Simplify using the standard rewrite rules. Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities.

